e Valley", "u": 0.44595, "v": 0.42929, "k": "region", "lat": 45.5815, "lon": -110.5692}, {"n": "Tom Miner Basin", "u": 0.12222, "v": 0.77735, "k": "region", "lat": 45.1847, "lon": -110.9538}, {"n": "Yankee Jim Canyon", "u": 0.16651, "v": 0.76706, "k": "region", "lat": 45.1966, "lon": -110.9012}, {"n": "Devils Slide", "u": 0.25135, "v": 0.85912, "k": "region", "lat": 45.0922, "lon": -110.7997}, {"n": "Crazy Mountains", "u": 0.6364, "v": 0.10525, "k": "region", "lat": 45.95, "lon": -110.34}, {"n": "Absaroka Range", "u": 0.62944, "v": 0.63274, "k": "region", "lat": 45.35, "lon": -110.35}, {"n": "Gallatin Range", "u": 0.12585, "v": 0.71996, "k": "region", "lat": 45.25, "lon": -110.95}, {"n": "Bridger Range", "u": 0.12972, "v": 0.21008, "k": "region", "lat": 45.83, "lon": -110.95}, {"n": "Boulder Plateau", "u": 0.79745, "v": 0.69389, "k": "region", "lat": 45.28, "lon": -110.15}], "tours": [{"id": "tominer", "name": "Tom Miner Basin", "blurb": "A hanging amphitheatre in the Gallatins where the forests are stone \u2014 redwood and sycamore, turned to agate in Absaroka ash.", "keys": [{"lat": 45.1847, "lon": -110.9538, "d": 10, "az": 250, "el": 15, "cap": "Tom Miner Basin, named for a prospector who found no gold here \u2014 the basin's treasure turned out to be older and stranger."}, {"lat": 45.16, "lon": -110.985, "d": 6, "az": 230, "el": 13, "cap": "The Gallatin Petrified Forest: fifty million years ago Absaroka eruptions buried standing groves; the folio's volcanic purples explain the ledges the trees weather out of."}, {"lat": 45.1966, "lon": -110.9012, "d": 7, "az": 200, "el": 13, "cap": "Yankee Jim Canyon. James George blasted a toll road through in 1873 and charged every wagon bound for the new park \u2014 until the railroad ruined his monopoly."}, {"lat": 45.21, "lon": -110.904, "d": 9, "az": 180, "el": 14, "cap": "Point of Rocks, where the canyon opens north into Paradise Valley \u2014 the sheet's whole story in one view."}]}, {"id": "branch", "name": "The Park Branch", "blurb": "Livingston to Cinnabar, 1883 \u2014 the railroad that turned a survey corridor into the road to Wonderland.", "keys": [{"lat": 45.6624, "lon": -110.561, "d": 10, "az": 170, "el": 16, "cap": "Livingston, born 1882 as a Northern Pacific division point. The branch to the park leaves the main line here; the shops built the town."}, {"lat": 45.47, "lon": -110.63, "d": 18, "az": 195, "el": 15, "cap": "Up Paradise Valley \u2014 ranches on the river terraces, Emigrant Peak ahead, the Absarokas walling the east. The 1891 sheet draws the rails all the way down."}, {"lat": 45.098, "lon": -110.7885, "d": 8, "az": 160, "el": 13, "cap": "Cinnabar, end of track 1883\u20131902 \u2014 a terminus town under the Devils Slide, whose red streak the sheet's geologists colored Chugwater. Nothing of Cinnabar remains."}, {"lat": 45.0319, "lon": -110.7058, "d": 7, "az": 150, "el": 14, "cap": "Gardiner, at the park's north gate. The rails reached it in 1902; Roosevelt laid the arch's cornerstone the next spring."}]}, {"id": "emigrant", "name": "Emigrant Gulch", "blurb": "Gold in '64, a ghost city by '70, hot water ever since.", "keys": [{"lat": 45.3702, "lon": -110.7335, "d": 9, "az": 140, "el": 15, "cap": "Emigrant, on the valley floor \u2014 stage stop, then siding, for the diggings in the gulch behind."}, {"lat": 45.3377, "lon": -110.6922, "d": 6, "az": 120, "el": 13, "cap": "Chico and its hot springs \u2014 the miners' boarding camp that outlived the mines; the springs rise where the folio's faults break the valley edge."}, {"lat": 45.31, "lon": -110.65, "d": 6, "az": 110, "el": 15, "cap": "Up the gulch: Thomas Curry struck placer gold in 1864, and Yellowstone City briefly held a thousand people. The high bars paid; the lode never quite did."}, {"lat": 45.2629, "lon": -110.7071, "d": 9, "az": 210, "el": 17, "cap": "Emigrant Peak, 10,921 ft \u2014 the valley's landmark, an Absaroka volcanic pile the folio paints in breccia browns."}]}, {"id": "boulder", "name": "Up the Boulder", "blurb": "From McLeod past the Natural Bridge to Independence \u2014 the mining road into the heart of the plateau country.", "keys": [{"lat": 45.6627, "lon": -110.116, "d": 9, "az": 185, "el": 15, "cap": "McLeod, where the West Boulder meets the main stem \u2014 a post office since 1886, and the gateway up the canyon."}, {"lat": 45.532, "lon": -110.214, "d": 7, "az": 190, "el": 14, "cap": "The Natural Bridge, where the Boulder once ran under its own limestone roof \u2014 the span fell in 1988, but the falls still vanish into the rock in low water."}, {"lat": 45.38, "lon": -110.22, "d": 11, "az": 195, "el": 15, "cap": "The canyon between the plateaus \u2014 Boulder Plateau east, East Boulder Plateau west \u2014 two-hundred-foot contours stacked like shingles."}, {"lat": 45.2124, "lon": -110.2463, "d": 7, "az": 200, "el": 14, "cap": "Independence, at the head of the road: a gold camp of the 1890s, snowbound half the year, quiet by 1904. The folio's economic sheet keys its veins."}]}, {"id": "crazies", "name": "The Island Range", "blurb": "The Crazies rise alone off the sheet's north edge \u2014 a sacred place of the Aps\u00e1alooke, and the valley's weather-maker.", "keys": [{"lat": 45.94, "lon": -110.33, "d": 16, "az": 340, "el": 17, "cap": "The southern Crazy Mountains \u2014 an igneous island in a sea of Cretaceous plains, standing apart from every range around it. To the Aps\u00e1alooke (Crow) they are Awaxaawipp\u00edia, a fasting and vision place; the sheet's east edge still carried their reservation line in 1891."}, {"lat": 45.8869, "lon": -110.6038, "d": 12, "az": 45, "el": 15, "cap": "Clyde Park and the Shields \u2014 hay and cattle country named for the river Clark's man John Shields followed in 1806."}, {"lat": 45.758, "lon": -110.2566, "d": 8, "az": 310, "el": 13, "cap": "Hunters Hot Springs, the territory's grand spa \u2014 Dr. Hunter claimed the waters in 1864, and the hotel drew trainloads from Springdale siding."}, {"lat": 45.6624, "lon": -110.561, "d": 11, "az": 270, "el": 16, "cap": "Back to Livingston under the range's standing wind \u2014 the town where every trip through this country begins and ends."}]}], "mines": [{"n": "Alice C.", "u": 0.43893, "v": 0.67974, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Amit No. 5", "u": 0.70994, "v": 0.71987, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Bar Group", "u": 0.36225, "v": 0.76686, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Black Warrior", "u": 0.95547, "v": 0.895, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Boulder Creek Mine", "u": 0.84871, "v": 0.49784, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Bull Elk Lode", "u": 0.9742, "v": 0.89103, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Carlton", "u": 0.98192, "v": 0.9113, "c": "lead"}, {"n": "Copper Group", "u": 0.44429, "v": 0.69056, "c": "copper"}, {"n": "Crevasse Mtn.", "u": 0.43281, "v": 0.89662, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Daisy", "u": 0.73945, "v": 0.74538, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Duke Mine", "u": 0.97119, "v": 0.91769, "c": "silver"}, {"n": "Emigrant", "u": 0.36315, "v": 0.69141, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Forgotten Mine", "u": 0.33161, "v": 0.65666, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Galena Queen", "u": 0.40158, "v": 0.71587, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Gish Mine", "u": 0.75235, "v": 0.52021, "c": "copper"}, {"n": "Hope Group", "u": 0.34421, "v": 0.70283, "c": "silver"}, {"n": "Jardine", "u": 0.40471, "v": 0.89659, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Jardine Mine", "u": 0.40241, "v": 0.88047, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Josephine Mine", "u": 0.93634, "v": 0.89465, "c": "silver"}, {"n": "Kreiger", "u": 0.4426, "v": 0.90445, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Lower Pine Creek", "u": 0.40103, "v": 0.87241, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Lulu Mine", "u": 0.95787, "v": 0.87204, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Magnitite Group", "u": 0.31053, "v": 0.72888, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Mclaren Mine", "u": 0.95821, "v": 0.88305, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Mohawk Warrior", "u": 0.98789, "v": 0.9278, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Pete Pear Group", "u": 0.36247, "v": 0.77979, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Pratt", "u": 0.40703, "v": 0.90442, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Red Fox", "u": 0.71218, "v": 0.53429, "c": "gold"}, {"n": "Red Fox Mine", "u": 0.71223, "v": 0.54475, "c": "